invariant: INV-16
file: p256_wide_point.c
catches: p256_equiv_test
reason: the doubling leaves out the last of Algorithm 6's 34 steps, the
  second doubling of Z3, so Z is half what the formula gives and the
  result is another point. No fault follows: every coordinate is still a
  field element. bin/p256_equiv_test holds the doubling to the complete
  addition of a point with itself on multiples of the generator and on
  the point at infinity.

--- old
    p256_wide_fe_add(&z3, &z3, &z3);
    p256_wide_fe_add(&z3, &z3, &z3);
--- new
    p256_wide_fe_add(&z3, &z3, &z3);
